Cooks use kosher salt because it is a coarse, flaky salt that is ideal for seasoning and adding flavor to dishes. It has a finer grain than table salt, which allows it to dissolve quickly and evenly in water, making it perfect for use in recipes that require precise measurements. Additionally, kosher salt does not contain any anti-caking agents or other additives that could affect the taste of a dish. It also has a purer flavor than table salt, making it a popular choice among professional chefs. Finally, because it is less processed than table salt, it retains more of its natural minerals and trace elements which can add additional health benefits to a dish. For these reasons, many cooks prefer to use kosher salt in their recipes. 
